Benchmark-client overlay for the pods (2026-10-26): the pod copies of serving.py / session_replay.py / tracelab.py plus
the Crossflow-style timestamp-window TraceLab replay (--tracelab-window-start-s / -window-s / -time-scale /
-window-rounds segment, start-at-timestamps scheduling) and the natural-text token source (--tracelab-text-source);
session_concurrency.py is the pod copy, unchanged. Tests: drivers/serving/test_tracelab_window.py. Deploy all four
together into $W/up/python/sglang/benchmark/ (tracelab.py into datasets/).

Deploy checklist (2026-10-28, learned the hard way on a re-provisioned cluster):
1. Copy serving.py, session_replay.py, session_concurrency.py into $W/up/python/sglang/benchmark/.
2. Copy tracelab.py into $W/up/python/sglang/benchmark/datasets/.
3. REGISTER the dataset in $W/up/python/sglang/benchmark/datasets/__init__.py -- step 2 alone is not enough, and the
   agent client then fails with "ValueError: Unknown dataset: tracelab-claude" while the chat client succeeds:
     from sglang.benchmark.datasets.tracelab import TraceLabClaudeDataset
     DATASET_MAPPING["tracelab-claude"] = TraceLabClaudeDataset
4. Run the client against UPSTREAM's tree (mn_bench.sh BENCH_PY defaults to $W/up/python). The overlay imports
   sglang.srt.utils.network, which our serving tree predates, so it cannot run on our tree.
5. Verify: PYTHONPATH=$W/up/python python -c 'from sglang.benchmark.datasets import DATASET_MAPPING as M; M["tracelab-claude"]'
6. EXTEND upstream's DatasetRow (sglang/benchmark/datasets/common.py): the overlay's TraceLab loader passes
   session-replay fields upstream's dataclass lacks, and the agent client fails with
   "TypeError: DatasetRow.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'session_id'". Add, all with defaults so no
   other loader changes: warmup_only: bool = False, session_id: Optional[str] = None,
   round_index: Optional[int] = None, inter_round_delay_s: float = 0.0 (timestamp already exists).
7. DRY-RUN the agent client before any smoke arm (seconds, no servers): call the client's own cli_main with the
   agent arguments and run_benchmark replaced by a stub that calls get_dataset and exits. Expected on the 24
   superposed windows at alpha 3: 13,353 rows / 324 sessions / 281 warmups. Each of the deployment gaps above
   cost a 15-minute smoke run to find; the dry-run finds all of them at once.
